Files taken verbatim
--------------------
    Simulation/SO101/so101_new_calib.urdf   -> tools/upstream/so101_new_calib.urdf
    Simulation/SO101/so101_old_calib.urdf   -> tools/upstream/so101_old_calib.urdf
    Simulation/SO101/assets/*.stl           -> meshes/arm/*.stl   (13 files)

The two .urdf files are kept unmodified under tools/upstream/ specifically so
this vendoring stays auditable and diffable against future upstream releases.

Modifications
-------------
Per the Apache-2.0 requirement to state changes, the following were made. None
alter the geometry: every origin, limit and inertia value in urdf/arm.xacro is
carried across byte-for-byte from so101_new_calib.urdf by a text-level
transform (tools/gen_arm_xacro.py), which then re-parses its own output and
asserts that the link set, joint names, joint types, limits and origins still
match upstream.

  1. Converted to a xacro macro (`so101_arm`) taking prefix/parent/origin.
  2. Link names prefixed with `arm_` to avoid colliding with this robot's own
     `base_link`. JOINT NAMES ARE DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED.
  3. Mesh paths rewritten from relative `assets/` references to
     `package://mmr_pkg/meshes/arm/`.
  4. Collision geometry re-pointed from the full-detail visual meshes to
     convex decompositions under `meshes/collision/arm/`, generated with CoACD
     by tools/arm_collision.py. The STL files themselves are unmodified.
  5. Six ROS 1 `<transmission>` blocks dropped (ROS 2 uses `<ros2_control>`).
  6. A stray `<origin>` element inside `<link name="gripper_frame_link">`
     dropped; it is not valid URDF and is ignored by parsers regardless.

